  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 802.01 Conservation easement",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-05-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 802.01 “Conservation easement” means a legal agreement between a landowner and a land trust or governmental agency that permanently limits uses of the land in order to protect its conservation values.\n\nSource. #8062, eff 3-13-04; ss by #8341, eff 4-25-05 (See Revision Note at chapter heading of Env-Wt 800); ss by #8762, INTERIM, eff 11-21-06, EXPIRED: 5-20-07\n\nNew. #8911, eff 6-20-07; ss by #11000, eff 2-1-16; ss by #12808, eff 12-15-19 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wt 800)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt800.html"
